        "source_text_sha256": "97e06b715ec15879e9da76b05cd5250edc5df0b287c0736c121fbebff2f7fc41",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Within an hour the three galleys were under way to \nMiletus, crammed with men. The first contained \nCesar and his friend Cinna, together with the freed- \nman Gallo and the two slaves, Cotta and Milo. All \nexcept Cesar himself showed great joy in at length \nfinding themselves on their way to liberty again. \nThey had been thirty-eight days with the pirates, so \nhard a task had it been for Gallo and the other slaves \nof Cesar to collect the sum of fifty talents. The \nproperty both of Cesar and his wife Cornelia had \nbeen confiscated by Sulla, who was then tyrant at \nRome; but Czsar had many rich kinsmen and friends.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
