      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-f4384e94db6cb569f845",
        "file": "greatpiratesstor0000jose_greatpiratesstor0000jose_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Great pirate stories. Second series",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/greatpiratesstor0000jose",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "1925-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "97e06b715ec15879e9da76b05cd5250edc5df0b287c0736c121fbebff2f7fc41",
        "evidence_excerpt": "At the time I speak of, Hong-Kong was a hot-bed \nof piracy and villany. Chinamen generally, but Can- \ntonese particularly—and of all Chinamen I suppose \nthere are no greater rascals—who had made their own \ncountry too hot for them, congregated on this rocky \npiece of English soil for protection. The Chinese \npopulation was then about 115,000. Headmen of \npirate gangs resided there, and piratical junks an- \nchored with impunity in the harbour; they used actually \nto have the coolness to come to, and take up a berth \nclose to my gun-boat, but usually they remained \namongst their fellow-craft at the other end of the \nharbour. An English brig, or schooner, or the smal- \nlest, most insignificant craft sailing under these \nvaunted colours, on anchoring in this English port, \nwas at once boarded, by not only one authority, but by \ntwo or three; certainly by the harbour-master and the \nguard-boat of some man-of-war at anchor in the port. \nShe had to sign papers, deliver others, and generally \ngive an account of herself, her whole crew, arms, con-",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/greatpiratesstor0000jose",
          "source_file": "greatpiratesstor0000jose_greatpiratesstor0000jose_djvu.txt",
