      {
        "finding_id": "section-96b0dd49125b39a0ffbc",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "It was the age of the galley, the oar-propelled \nvessel which moved independently of the wind in \nthe fine-weather months of the great inland sea. \nTherefore to the dwellers on the coast the Sea- \nwolves were a perpetual menace ; as, when booty \nwas unobtainable at sea, they raided the towns \nand villages of their Christian foes. During all \nthe period here dealt with no man’s life, no \nwoman’s honour, was safe from these pirates within \nthe area of their nefarious activities. They held \nthe Mediterranean in fee, they levied toll on all \nwho came within reach of their galleys and their \nscimitars. Places unknown to the geography of \nthe sixteenth century became notorious in their \nday, and Christian wives and mothers learned to \ntremble at the very names of Algiers and Tunis. \nFrom these places the rovers issued to capture, to \ndestroy, and to enslave: in Oran and Tlemcen, in \nTenes, Shershell, Bougie, Jigelli, Bizerta, Sfax, \nSusa, Monastir, Jerbah, and Tripoli they lurked \nready for the raid and the foray. At one time \nall Northern Africa would thrill to the triumph \nof the Moslem arms, at another there would go \nup the wail of the utterly defeated ; but in spite \nof alternations of fortune the Sea-wolves abode \nin the localities of their choice, and ended in \nestablishing those pirate States which troubled \nthe peace of the Mediterranean practically until \nthe introduction of steam.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
