      {
        "finding_id": "section-998cf02da8a82a9df43f",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "There was so much history made at this period, \nthe stage of world politics was occupied by so \nmany great, striking, and dazzling personalities, \nthat the Sea-wolves and all they accomplished \nwere to a great extent overshadowed by happen- \nings which the chroniclers of the time considered \nto be of greater importance. In this no doubt \nthey were right in the main; but, in spite of this \nopinion which they held, we find that time and \nagain the main stream of events is ruffled by the \nprows of the pirate galleys. Such men as the \nBarbarossas, as Dragut, and Ali Basha could \nonly have been suppressed and exterminated had \nthe whole might of Christendom been turned \nagainst them, for they held in their hands two \nweapons, the keenest ard most powerful with \nwhich to attain the objects which they had in view.",
