      {
        "finding_id": "section-d7e0d62c89a58ffbd55d",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "This period has been called “The Grand Period \nof the Moslem Corsairs”” because it was in some- \nthing less than a century, from the year of the \nexpulsion of the Moors from Granada in 1492 to \nthe death of Ali Basha in 1580, that the Sea- \nwolves were at the height of their power, that the \npiratical States of the Mediterranean were in the \nmaking. That subsequently they gave great cause \nof trouble to Christendom is written in characters \nof blood and fire throughout the history of the \nsucceeding centuries ; but the real interest in the \ncareers of these men resides in the fact that they \nestablished, by their extraordinary aptitude for sea- \nadventure, the permanent place which was held \nby their descendants. Time and again in the \nsixteenth century the effort was made to destroy \nthem root and branch: they were defeated, driven \nout of their strongholds on shore, crushed apparently \nforever. But nothing short of actual extermination \ncould have been successful in this; as, no matter \nhow severe had been the set-back, there was always \nleft a nucleus of the pirates which in a short time \ngrew again into a formidable force. The Ottoman \nTurk, magnificent fighter as he was on land, \nseemed to lose his great qualities when the venue \nwas changed from the land to the sea. The \nJanissaries, that picked corps trained as few soldiers \nwere trained even in that age of iron, who never",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 19453,
          "end_char": 20855,
          "start_line": 749,
          "end_line": 776,
