        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "There is very little doubt that critics will point \nout that the corsairs were by no means universally \nsuccessful ; that, as in the case of the attack by \nHassem, the ruler of Algiers in 1563, on Oran and \nMarzaquivir (a small port in the immediate vicinity \nof Oran), in the end the Moslems were badly \nbeaten. This undoubtedly was the case, and there \nis no desire to magnify the deeds of the Sea- \nwolves or to minimise the heroic defence of Mar- \nzaquivir by the Count of Alcaudete, or that of \nOran by his brother, Don Martin de Cordoba. At \nthe last moment of their wonderful defence they \nwere relieved by a fleet sent by the King of Spain, \nand Hassem had to abandon his artillery, ammuni- \ntion, and stores and beat a hasty retreat to the \nplace from whence he had come.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
