        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Of the corsairs dealt with in this record of their \ndeeds the two Barbarossas were the sons of a \nMohammedan father and a Christian mother. \nDragut Reis was a pure Mohammedan, and Ali \nBasha was a pure-blooded Italian. All these men, \nas will be seen, raised themselves to eminence \nin the profession of piracy; in each and every \nseparate case starting at the very bottom rung of \nthe ladder and rising, by sheer stress of valour and \ncharacter, to the very top. Each in turn became \nAdmiralissimo to the Grand Turk at Constantinople. \nKheyr-ed-Din Barbarossa commanded the Ottoman \nfleet at the great battle of Prevesa, at which he \nmet with his life-long competitor at sea, the famous \nGenoese Admiral, Andrea Doria. Dragut Reis \nwas killed at the siege of Malta in 1565, and Ali \nBasha was the only Moslem commander who",
