        "evidence_excerpt": "It was one of the cruellest of ages, and rough \ncruelty was the principal means adopted to ensure \nsuccess ; sheer terror was the weapon of the leader. \nThus when one Hassan, a subordinate of Kheyr- \ned-Din, failed to take a Spanish ship because she \nmade too stout a resistance, his chief caused him \nto be soundly flogged and then thrown into prison. \nSuch methods naturally raised up hosts of enemies \nin the wake of the piratical commanders, ready \nat any time to do them a mortal injury, and it",
