        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "It is the autocrat who is made by the circum- \nstances of his life who ultimately becomes supreme. \nThe leaders among the corsairs were tried by every \ntest of prosperity and of adverse fortune; they \nemerged from the ruck in the first instance because \nit was in them to display a more desperate valour \nthan did their contemporaries, and it was only \nwhen they emerged triumphant from this, the \nfirst test, that they could begin to impose their \nwill upon others. It was then that their real \ntrials began, as the undisciplined are ever prone \nto suspicion, much given to murmuring against \na leader who is not perpetually successful.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
