      {
        "finding_id": "section-f9038d35c2c5231f9423",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "In the year 1457 an obscure Roumelian or Albanian \nrenegado named Mahomedi was banished from \nConstantinople by the Grand Turk ; he established \nhimself in the island of Mitylene and there mar- \nried a Christian widow named Catalina, by whom \nhe had two sons, Uruj and Khizr. The father had \nbeen a sailor and both sons adopted the same pro- \nfession. It is from the pages of El Maestro Don \nFray Prudencio de Sandoval that we glean these \nbare facts concerning the birth and parentage of \nthese men who, in after-years, became known to all \nthe dwellers on the shores of the Mediterranean as \nthe “ Barbarossas,” from their red beards. Sandoval, \nBishop of Pampluna, published in the year 1614 \nhis monumental history of the Emperor Charles V., \nand through his splendid volumes the deeds of the \nMoslem corsairs run like the scarlet thread which \nis twisted through a Government rope. It is \nevident that the fact of having to deal with such \nrascals annoys the good Bishop not a little, as his \nsevere and caustic comments frequently display. \nThere was incident and accident enough in the life \nof the famous “ Carlos Quinto” without the historian",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1614
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 76551,
          "end_char": 77702,
          "start_line": 2166,
          "end_line": 2188,
