        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "But when storm and rain gave way to the smooth \nwaters and balmy breezes, the Sea-wolves were \ncertain of their prey, as the whole length and \nbreadth of the tideless sea was sure to be filled \nwith the ships of the detested Christians trafficking \nin every direction. In the ethics of the Moslem \nall ships which sailed under the banner of the \nCross, no matter to what nation they belonged, \nwere fair game, even supposing that her insignia \nwere the Crescent—well, supposing the spot to be \nsufficiently remote, dead men tell no tales, and the \npirates were to be trusted to see to it that none \nescaped.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
