        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "In a simultaneous, and as we have seen a con- \ncerted attack, the beaks of the galleys crushed into \nthe broadsides of The Galley of Naples, and, ever \nforemost in the fray, Uruj and Kheyr-ed-Din were \nthe first two men to board. Then, when men were \nhand to hand and foot to foot, when Moslem \nscimitar rang on Christian sabre, and the air was \nfilled with the oaths and shouts of the combatants, \nthe third remaining pirate craft grappled The Galley \nof Naples by the stern, and a tide of fresh, un- \nwounded men burst into the fray. This was the",
