          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "THE events recorded in the last chapter bring us \ndown to the end of the year 1515, and while every \nendeavour has been made to present affairs in \nchronological sequence, it must be remembered \nthat the dates of piratical expeditions are often \nimpossible to obtain: the wrath of the chroniclers \nat the nefarious deeds of the corsairs greatly ex- \nceeding their desire for a meticulous accuracy in \nthe matter of the exact time of their occurrence. \nUruj, as has been seen, had by his headstrong folly \nonce again placed his brother and himself in a \ndecidedly awkward situation. By the losses which \nhe had incurred in his second ill-advised attempt \non Bougie he had so weakened the piratical con- \nfederation that the countenance of some potentate \nhad again become necessary for their continued \nexistence, and the Sultan of Tunis had now re- \npudiated all connection with these ingrates.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
