        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "century the Grand Turk was in every sense “ far \naway ” from the struggling corsairs on the littoral \nof Northern Africa, and was a sovereign of such \ngreat and mysterious might that any man with a \nless fine instinct into the psychology of the times \nin which he lived than Kheyr-ed-Din would have \nhesitated long and anxiously before addressing him \ndirectly ; would probably in the end not have done \nso at all. But desperate diseases require desperate \nremedies, and the politic corsair well knew that \neven the moral support of such an one as the Sultan \nof Constantinople was worth more than even \nmaterial aid from a Sultan of Tunis.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
