      {
        "finding_id": "section-359a1d00cea36a394b39",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The corsair had to be armed at all points, in \nthe moral as well as the material sense, as he was \nthe enemy of all men, and all were vowed to his \ndestruction. Every cruise which he took raised \nup against him fresh hatred and a more bitter \nanimus, and we must remember that it was not \nonly men individually, but Principalities and \nPowers that were arrayed in line of battle for \nhis destruction. At the present juncture Spain \nwas specially hostile, for not only had her pos- \nsession of Bougie been twice attacked by the Sea- \nwolves, but a valuable convoy had been captured. \nAn expedition, in consequence, was sent by the \nSpaniards against the Barbarossas, but this effort \ndid not result in much damage being done to the \noffenders. The Spaniards destroyed four piratical \nvessels which had been abandoned by their crews \nat Bizerta, and pushed a strong reconnaissance into \nthe Bay of Tunis itself. Here shots were exchanged \nbetween the Spanish fleet and the forts—under \nwhich Kheyr-ed-Din had drawn up his ships—and \nthe Spaniards then abandoned the enterprise and \nreturned from whence they had come.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 107686,
          "end_char": 108801,
          "start_line": 2933,
          "end_line": 2955,
