        "evidence_excerpt": "By his side was his faithful lieutenant Venalcadi. \nIn a breathless mélée Christian sword and Moslem \nsabre clashed and rang. His turban gone, his \ngreat curved scimitar red to the hilt, the undaunted \ncorsair fought his last fight as became the terror \nof his name. Almost had he succeeded in breaking \nthrough the ring of his foes when Garzia de Tineo, \nalferez (or lieutenant) to Captain Diego de An- \ndrade, wounded him severely with a pike. Uruj",
