        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "stumbled, was struck on the head with another \nweapon ; he reeled and fell. The fight was over, \nand one of the Barbarossas bit the dust. Garzia \nde Tineo leaped upon the fallen man and cut off \nhis head. It is recorded that Garzia de Tineo was \nwounded in the finger by Uruj in the course of the \ncombat, and that for the rest of his life he proudly \nexhibited the scar as a sign that it was none other \nthan he who had killed the famous corsair.",
