        "evidence_excerpt": "Republics, and all the time was in touch with \nthe Sea-wolves, who swarmed on the coasts of \nAfrica, and lurked in every creek and harbour \nof the Ionian Sea. “In all the bloody hazards \nof his life,” to quote once again the words of the \nGrand Turk, “he could, in the end, depend more \nor less on the corsairs, whether they ostensibly \nsailed beneath his banner or whether they did \nnot, as when danger threatened what name was \nso potent as that of Barbarossa, which his followers \nasserted to be worth ten thousand men, when \nshouted on the day of battle!”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
