        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "had placed on his own head the iron crown of \nLombardy ; his viceroys ruled in Naples and Sicily, \nhis dukes and feudatories in Florence and Ferrara, \nin Mantua and in Milan; there was no more Italy. \nAll these recent acquisitions had been rendered \npossible by the defection of Andrea Doria, the \nGenoese seaman, from Francis I. of France to the \nside of the Emperor. From henceforward it was \nagainst this modern Cesar that Barbarossa had to \ncontend; the monarch under whose’ banner \nswarmed the terrible Schwartz-Reiters of Germany, \nfor whose honour marched the incomparable in- \nfantry of Spain, for whom the fleets of the gallant \nGenoese sailed in battle-array under the orders of \nthe greatest admiral of the day, Andrea Doria. \nAll these disciplined legions of Christendom were \narrayed against the corsair king ; banded together \nfor the destruction of that daring pirate whose flag \nfloated in insolent triumph above the white walls \nof Algiers.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
