        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Thus balked of his prey, Barbarossa swung his \nfleet round to the southward and westward and \nsailed for Sardinia, where, from the Straits of \nBonifacio to Cape Spartivento, he left no house \nstanding that would burn, or man alive who was \nnot swept in as a captive. The descent of the \ncorsairs in force, such as Kheyr-ed-Din now had \nat his disposal, was one of the most awful calamities \nfor a country that it is possible to imagine. When",
