        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "begun or finished at the time of Paul IIL, have \nnothing to do with the sack of 1527, with the \nConnétable de Bourbon, or with the Emperor \nCharles V. All the bastions, that of the Belvedere \nexcepted, point towards the sea-coast, which was \nperpetually harried and terrified by Turkish or \nBarbary pirates. These would appear with lightning- \nlike rapidity in more than one place at a time, and \ncarry off as many unfortunate men, women, and \nchildren as they could collect. . . . To prevent \nthe recurrence of such disasters the sea-coast was \nlined with watch-towers, the guns of which could \nwarn the peasants of the approach of suspicious \nvessels.”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
