      {
        "finding_id": "section-2af8503297a1a02d1242",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "We must now return, however, to that eagle \nwho fluttered so sorely the dovecotes, both Christian \nand Moslem, and whose loudly proclaimed faith in \nthe Prophet never permitted his religion to stand \ninconveniently in the way of his material advance- \nment in the world. The soldiers and sailors of the \ncorsair entered Bizerta shouting for Soliman and \nBarbarossa. There was no mention of Raschid, \nthat Prince of the Hafsit dynasty, whom Kheyr- \ned-Din had declared to the townspeople he had \ncome to restore to the throne of his ancestors. \nToo late the town sprang to arms, under a chief \nnamed Abdahar, and in the first instance accom- \nplished a considerable success. Barbarossa’s men \nwere unprepared, and a number of them were \nslain. Driven into a bastion of the walls, a party \nof the corsairs were desperately defending them- \nselves, when one Baetio, a Spanish renegado, \ndiscovered that a cannon behind them pointing sea- \nwards was loaded. He succeeded, with the assist- \nance of others, in slewing it round and discharged \nit at close quarters into the packed masses of the \nenemy. This caused a frightful demoralisation to \nset in; the corsairs rallied and soon swept all before \nthem. The massacre turned from the one side to \nthe other, and it is said that no less than three \nthousand of the unfortunate townspeople were slain. \nBarbarossa only called off his men when they were \nwearied out by the slaughter.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 231586,
          "end_char": 233014,
          "start_line": 6101,
          "end_line": 6129,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
