      {
        "finding_id": "section-93fffd05871333a76b25",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "There was no artifice left untried by the despot \nof Tunis. To the African princes, Moors as well \nas Arabs and Berbers, did Kheyr-ed-Din send \nembassies. For these he chose cunning men well \nversed in the means of exciting the furious passions \nof these primitive and ferocious peoples, and it \nwas their mission to represent Muley Hassan as \nan infamous apostate who was prompted by am- \nbition and revenge, not only to become the vassal \nof a Christian king, but to conspire with him to \nextirpate the Mohammedan faith. The subtle \npolicy inflamed these ignorant and bigoted Mo- \nhammedans to the point of madness, and from \nfar and near they threw in their lot with the man \nwho represented himself to be the rallying-point \nfor all those in Africa who desired not only to \npreserve their holy religion but also their personal \nliberty. From Tripoli and Jerba, from Bougie and \nBona, from the shores of Shott-el-Jerid, through \nall the dim hinterland that stretches from thence \nnorth-westwards to Algiers, the tribesmen came \nflocking in. The wild riders of the desert had \nbeen rounded up, and it is said that no less than \ntwenty thousand horsemen, in addition to an in- \nnumerable crowd of infantry, responded to the \ncall of the master schemer who was but using \nthese guileless savages to further his own personal \nends. The land-pirates of the desert, those stormy",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
          "source_file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
