        "evidence_excerpt": "Muley Hassan had exchanged the comparatively \ndignified position of a prince in exile, who has been \nexpropriated by the strong hand, for that of the \npuppet of one of the greatest enemies of his religion. \nNeither he nor his people were one whit the better \nfor the change, and, as, far as vassalage was con- \ncerned, they would in all probability, in the state of \nreligious feeling at the time, have sooner been \nsubordinate to the Moslem corsair than to the \nChristian King.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
