        "evidence_excerpt": "unexampled cruelty, a prototype of those other \ncorsair kings by whom he was succeeded. But the \nreal source of his power Jay, not in stone walls and \nfortifications, nor in ill-trained levies of African \ntribes, but in his own genius for command at sea, \nand the manner in which he was able to inspire \nwith his own dauntless and desperate spirit those \nhardy mariners who followed in his train, the \ndescendants of the “ Moriscoes ” who hailed from \nthe ancient Moorish kingdoms of Cordoba and \nGranada.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
