        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "been, and that they would have gone in and burnt \nor disabled the galleys of the corsair, slain their \nleader, or driven him ashore. Hot on the tracks \nof Adan Centurion and his nephew John came \nthe veteran Andrea Doria with forty galleys, but \nhe was too late, and the bird had flown; had it \nbeen he who had arrived in the first instance, then \nit is more than probable that matters would have \nturned out differently, and Kheyr-ed-Din had then \nand there terminated his career. It is true that \nAndrea possessed himself of Bona, and the Corsair \nKing was shorn of yet another of his land-stations, \nbut for the time he had cut himself adrift from \nthe land, and had gone back to that element in \nwhich he was particularly at home.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
