        "evidence_excerpt": "Doria, Grimani, and Capello had now nearly \n200 ships carrying nearly 60,000 men. Such \na force, in all ages, has been considered great. \nWilliam the Conqueror conquered Britain with a \nless number; it is almost half the total of the \npersonnel of the British fieet in the present day \nwhich has to defend a country with 40,000,000 \ninhabitants, and all this force had been raised, \narmed, and equipped to combat with a Moslem \ncorsair.",
