        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "But “the corsair” kept. his head, and kept his \ntemper, and saved the Ottoman fleet for his master \nfrom his great rival, Doria. That noble Genoese \nseaman was for once in his life “letting I dare \nnot wait upon I would” ; he would not order the \nattack for which his men were waiting, and no \nprovocation, apparently, could tempt Barbarossa",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
