        "evidence_excerpt": "It is interesting to have a contemporary view of \nthe correct treatment of the galley slave from those \nwho had to do with him. In the case of the \ncorsairs and their adversaries the gallerians were \nas a rule prisoners of war, but as time went on and \nwars became less frequent than they were through- \nout the sixteenth century, another source of supply \nwas tapped by sending to the galleys the criminals \nof any country which desired to fill up the rowers’ \nbenches. In consequence there was always one \nthing which was feared above all others on board \na galley, and that was a rising of the slaves.",
