        "evidence_excerpt": "There were no longer among the Moors of \nAndalusia learned philosophers, expert mathema- \nticians, wise astronomers, and practical agriculturists; \nthere was among them but one art, one science, \none means of gaining a livelihood—the practice of \nwar—and their very existence depended on the \nspoils which could be reft from the hereditary enemy. \nThe corsair who grew to man’s estate, brought up \nin Algiers, Tunis, Tenes, Jerba, or any other of the \nlurking places in which the sea-wolves congregated, \nhad asa rule no chance but to follow the sea, to \nexist as his father had existed before him ; he must",
