        "evidence_excerpt": "The council of the town of “ Africa” troubled \nthemselves but little more concerning Dragut, his \nships, and his corsairs ; he had departed, and as the \ndays wore on and no further tidings of him came \nto hand, these simple folk thanked God that they \nwere rid of a knave and went about their usual \navocations as unconcernedly as if no sea-wolves \nlurked under the shadowed headlands of that con- \ntinent in which their homes were situated. They \nwere a people essentially of the land; although \nthey dwelt on the confines of the ocean the ways",
