        "evidence_excerpt": "and habits of those who earned a precarious living \non the waters were a sealed book to them, and with \nthe “ Africans” it was a case of “out of sight out \nof mind” so far as the corsairs were concerned. \nBut that black-hearted traitor Ibrahim Amburac \nand the few others who had been gained over by \nthe gold of Dragut watched and waited for the \nattack which they knew to be impending.",
