        "evidence_excerpt": "on the part of the pirates: a fresh hundred men, \nwho had hitherto taken no part in the combat, \nnow pressed to the front and formed the advance, \nthose who had been before engaged now forming \nthe supports; that which had been the shaft of \nthe spear now forming its head. With Dragut \nleading, these fresh unwounded men swept forward \nover the burning beam ; irresistible as some mighty \nriver in spate, these disciplined ruffians, headed by \nthis master spirit, burst through the ill-organised \nresistance opposed to them, and slew and slew \nand slew.",
