        "evidence_excerpt": "What passed between Dragut and the council \nof “ Africa,” who in so unqualified a manner had \nrefused that warrior as a citizen, is not on record ; \nall that we know is that the Moslem leader \ndispensed with their services, and did not invite his \nnew fellow-townsmen to share with him the burden \nof government. There was hurry in the admini- \nstration of the corsair states, as the form of rule \nwhich they adopted was apt to irk the rulers in \nChristendom. In this particular instance Dragut, \nhaving expelled the Spaniards from the coast towns, \nknew that a reckoning with the Emperor and his",
