      {
        "finding_id": "section-de026069b4f90337d444",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "While Dragut was pursuing his “ Horrid De- \nvastations,” Doria was not idle, but was ranging \nthe northern coast of Africa in his fruitless search ; \nin the course of this he landed at Cape Bona, on \nwhich was the castle of Calibia, held by the \ncorsairs ; these men, who were a portion of Dragut’s \nfollowing, made a most valiant defence; they \nwere, however, few in number, and when their \ncaptain was killed by the ball from an arquebus \nthey surrendered. Encouraged by this success, \nthe Christian fleet then stood along the coast to \ninspect “ Africa.” Sailing quite close to the shore \nthey came within range of the guns of the garrison, \nwho, under the direction of Aisa, were very much \non the alert. As the admiral’s galley at the \nhead of the line passed the walls of the town, she \nwas received with a hot fire, and one large cannon- \nball struck the stern of Doria’s ship, doing con- \nsiderable structural damage, and killing five of \nhis men. This occurrence took place in broad \ndaylight in, full view of all the garrison, who \nsignalled their delight at the discomfiture of their \nfoes by the noise of cymbals and atambours, and \nby wild and ferocious yells. Doria, who was in \nno position to land and make reprisals, fell into \nthe greatest paroxysm of fury, and we are told \nthat “he swore the destruction of that detested \ncity.”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
