        "evidence_excerpt": "Not only did the indefatigable corsair get clear \naway without any suspicion on the part of the \nadmiral, but his first act on gaining the open sea \nwas to capture the Patrona galley sent from Sicily \nby Don Juan de Vega to say that reinforcements \nwere on the road. In this ill-fated craft was \nBuguer, the son of Muley Hassan, King of Tunis, \nwho was sent as prize to Soliman at Constantinople, \nwhere the Sultan caused him to be shut up in the",
