      {
        "finding_id": "section-1a511e5a119d513cd554",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "With the remainder of the siege, which was yet \nto last till September 18th, we have no concern in \nthis book. It is only necessary to say that the men \nof Il Borgo were worthy to stand in the same \ncategory with the defenders of St. Elmo, which is \nequivalent to stating that in them also was dis- \ncovered the last limit of heroism. The Grand \nMaster survived the siege, his monument is the \nnoble city of “ Valetta” built on Mount Sceberras. \nThe Turks abandoned the siege and returned to \nConstantinople on the arrival of some insignificant \nreinforcements from Sicily. So terrible had been \nthe resistance of the Knights that no heart was left \nin their armada. Of Dragut there remains but \nlittle to be said: he was perhaps the best educated \nof the corsairs and less cruel than was usually their \nhabit. Although not so renowned as his more \ncelebrated master, Kheyr-ed-Din Barbarossa, this is, \nperhaps, because his career was cut short at the \nsiege of Malta at a comparatively early age. Al- \nthough he never attained the rank of Admiralissimo \nto the Grand Turk, that potentate, as we have seen, \nplaced in him the greatest confidence, and relied \nlargely on his judgment, especially when sea-affairs \nwere in question. Like the Barbarossas before \nhim, he rose from nothing to the height to which he",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
