        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Ali, being in no position to wage war in the desert \nagainst these people, had to swallow the insult \nand to turn his attention to regulating the internal \naffairs of his newly acquired kingdom. ‘This he suc- \nceeded in doing sufficiently by the month of June \nin the following year to enable him to leave Tunis \nin the hands of one Rabadan, a Sardinian renegado, \nand to start himself for Constantinople. His reason \nfor doing this was the old one of attempting to \nconsolidate his power in Northern Africa by ap- \npealing to the Sultan for help. As long as the \nGoletta remained in the hands of the Spaniards \nno corsair could feel himself secure in either Tunis \nor Algiers. The object of Ali was to beg from \nthe Grand Turk men and ships to assist him to \nchase the Spaniards out of Africa.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
