        "evidence_excerpt": "The corsair recognised that he could do no \nmore: sullenly he cast off the tow, and, forming \nup some thirty of his galleys, still in a condition \nto navigate, stood boldly through the centre of \nwhere the battle had once raged, and escaped. \nThe Capitana of Malta had been taken; and to \nthe Sultan did Occhiali present the great standard \nof Saint John, as an earnest of his achievement.",
