        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "However, the period 1500-1900 is also part of a much longer global history \nof piracy, which stretches from the formulation of the concept more than \ntwo thousand years ago up to the present. With regard to modern and \ncontemporary history, it is frequently observed that piracy is an essentially \nEuropean concept that has been, and in some cases still is, inappropriately \napplied to very different economic, social, political, and cultural contexts",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
