        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Similarly, the so-called Sea Peoples, who wreaked havoc in the eastern \nMediterranean between the fourteenth and twelfth centuries BCE, are often \nidentified as pirates. However, there is no reliable evidence that the Sea \nPeoples were pirates or were seen as such by their contemporaries, either \nexplicitly or implicitly. Piracy began to be conceptualized in the writings \nof Homer and later Greek texts, but the word peirates (eipatys) seems to \nhave appeared only around the mid-third century BCE.”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
