          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "This concept of the pirate established itself in legal traditions derived \nfrom Roman Law, but was extended in the medieval period by descrip- \ntions, in the writings of Bartolus of Saxoferrato? for instance, of the sea \nrobber as hostis humani generis. Canon Law further stamped the pirate \nas a heretic who must be expelled from the Christian community. In the \nBullae Coenae Domini, all pirates, corsairs, and sea robbers (omnes piratas, \ncursarios, ac latrunculos maritimos), and the receivers of their stolen goods",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
