        "evidence_excerpt": "It was the pirate who made the seas unsafe, “qui prius maria infestavit,’ as \nthe humanist lawyer Johannes Drosaeus put it in 1564.74 Time and again in \nthe Early Modern period, the restlessness of the pirate, the uninterrupted \nwandering from coast to coast, island to island, beyond the horizon, attracted \nparticular condemnation. The leading judge in the case against Joseph \nDawson and others accused of piracy in 1696 emphasized that the concept",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1696
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
