        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The court proceedings took place on 7 and 9 January 1675. The accused \nwere Cusack (“alias Dixon, alias Smith”) and six members of his crew.5? The \ncharge was piracy \"against the Law of Nations\" on account of the seizure \nofthe Robert and other ships.5^ Cusack defended himself by claiming that \nhe had only undertaken privateering raids as authorized by the letter of \nmarque issued by the French king. The court, however, insisted on not \nrecognizing the “French commission.\"5 After consulting for an hour, the",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1675
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
