        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "captured ought to have been examined by due process of law in a prize \ncourt. Cusack's accomplices knew this and in the interrogation into the wild \nplundering ofthe two Swedish vessels and the Danish ship each denied his \nown participation and tried to incriminate the others.59 These violations of \nthelaw were at the most necessary but by no means sufficient conditions for \ncondemnation as a pirate. Far weightier than these offences was the fact that \nCusack's international raids, by which the subjects of a number of nations \nwere affected, redounded upon the reputation of the English Crown and \nmust have negatively affected the relations of England with other countries.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
