      {
        "finding_id": "section-b5396b52834c8d0d8388",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Mist certainly exploited the critical potential of pirates and their com- \nmunities to cast veiled aspersions against the government of the Whig prime \nminister Robert Walpole (1676-1745), who, his critics alleged, had risen to \npower amid the financial scandal of the South Sea Bubble in 1720-1721 by \n\"screening\" those responsible from prosecution.'^ Mist made the point \nby alluding to the concurrence between pirate commonwealths and the \noriginal purposes of government, which, Mist explained, was \"founded upon \nCovenant; it was Mens agreeing to be governed according to their particular \njudgments, and particular Appetites, that first set up Commonwealths; and \nthey consented for the Benefits of Society, that any Man who injured another \nshould suffer such a Penalty.\" The problem in existing commonwealths was \nthat “those appointed to Preside\" grasped more power and by \"skreening\" \nthemselves from punishment, making “unworthy Promotions,” and practic- \ning \"Imbezzlement.\" The pirates, by contrast, “seem to be very jealous of \ntheir Liberties,\" and practice promotion by \"Merit.\" Although \"they are \nRogues to all the World besides\", Mist wrote, “yet they are Men of Honour \nto one another.\"",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1676
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
