        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "himself).” This rational model of self-interested piratical decision-making \nalso entailed “progressive racial practices,” such as liberating slaves taken at \nsea to maximize the “dispersed benefit” obtained by augmenting the crew.” \nThis rehabilitation of the hostis humani generis transforms the pirate into \na willing subject of political philosophical order. The pirate is no longer an \noutcast and a villain, but an active constituent of contractual government. \nThis analysis fails to grasp the historical function of piracy in Western \npolitical thought in circumscribing the problem of misgovernment.?? This \nwas exemplified in the political thought of the man whose writings have \ncome to symbolize British social contract theorizing, John Locke (1632-1704).",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1632
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
