      {
        "finding_id": "section-c80324bef4c5e1a69565",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "death in 1704. Throughout these years, Locke was closely involved with \nthe Board of Trade and its efforts to protect Britain’s maritime trade from \npiracy.** In the context of the Board's oversight not only of maritime trade, \nbut also of colonial governance and inter-imperial rivalry, Locke had the \nopportunity to meet the sometime pirates and privateers, William Dampier \n(1651-1715) and Lionel Wafer (1640-1705).*? Both claimed to have served \nin privateer crews under Letters of Marque from their sovereign to raid \nthe shipping of his Spanish and French enemies. But both also joined one \nof the various parties of buccaneers, who raided Spanish shipping and \ncommunities on their own piratical account on the Pacific and Caribbean \ncoast of the Isthmus of Panama. Locke owned copies of both Dampier's \nNew Voyage Round the World (1697) and Wafer's New Voyage and Description \nof the Isthmus of America (1699), which spoke of some of their piratical \nexperiences.5? More importantly, Locke also owned copies of the 1695 \nand 1699 editions of Alexandre Exquemelin's The Buccaneers of America \n(originally published in Dutch in 1678), the latter of which contained the \npublished journal of another English buccaneer and companion of Dampier \nand Wafer, Basil Ringrose. Although it was subsequently overshadowed by \nCaptain Charles Johnson's General History ofthe Pyrates published in 1724, \nExquemelin's book was written from first-hand experience in buccaneer \ncrews and was the most detailed account of pirate political organization \navailable in Locke's lifetime.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1640,
          1651,
          1678,
          1695,
          1697,
          1699
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
