        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Andrew Dilts has recently argued that the question of the appropriate \npunishment for those who transgress, renounce, or live beyond divine, \nmoral, and human law has shaped the Western “canon of political theory.””5 \nThe figure of the pirate, like that of the “savage,” is a “source of physical and \nontological threat\" to the law-abiding inhabitants of civil society. The pirate \nis one of those \"liminal figures that haunt the boundaries of membership \n[of civil society] and the border between the law of reason and the law of",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
