          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "This attention to nautical resources mattered to Pires as a measure both \nof commercial and of naval capacity. Yet, he also recognized the inextricable \nrelation of nautical resources to regional slavery. Some ofthe maritime com- \nmerce he described involved a trade in slaves, including captives acquired \nin maritime raiding and war. Such displaced people formed, among other \nthings, a source of maritime labour. Hence, piracy in early modern Southeast \nAsia, which included the taking of people, intertwined with the slave trade \nboth in its commercial aspect and as a source of maritime labour.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
