        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "and in Admiral Speelman's 1669 report, he did not level a specific charge \nor claim of piracy, but instead, cast aspersions on a nautical realm that \nhad challenged, and, for a time, helped to foil, his aims. Speelman's scorn \nwas essentially name-calling in the mode of history written by the victors.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1669
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
