      {
        "finding_id": "section-26c1810c11849aa5737d",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "this time, there was in place a conception of piracy in relation to sovereign \nauthority over the seas and the markets that absorbed clandestine goods, \non the part of regional rulers. Kanhoji himself, I would argue, represented \na shift, for he laid explicit claims to sovereignty over the seas and insisted \nthat only his passes were legal tender over specific stretches, and that the \nEnglish had no right to defy his sphere of influence. Unpacking his actions \nand his pronouncements as they come to us in the East India Company's \ndocumentation, it is clear that he embodied the political conceptions ofthe \nMaratha State and its understanding of sea power and that he set out initially \nas a privateer fighting on behalf of the Maratha ruling house before he set \nhimself up as a coastal potentate, acknowledging the sovereign authority \nof his overlord but having marked his sphere of influence. Standing up \nfor his sovereign's rights against the claims of other coastal rulers like the \nSidis of Janjora and the dispersed Portuguese power off Goa and Bassein, \nthe Desais of Sawantvadi, he claimed to be lord of the seas with definite \nrights. His death and the subsequent destruction of his small state by the \nBombay Marine, the naval force ofthe English East India Company, put an \nend to the experiment, but one important and noticeable consequence was \nthe dispersal of piratical activity along the coast, especially its northern \nstretches, the area of our present study.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
