      {
        "finding_id": "section-920be22b468f58aa9a36",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "presence of the Dwarka shrine in Okhamandal and the influence it enjoyed, \nthe participation ofthe temple in the proceeds of piracy made an impression \non early observers, even on Colonel Walker, who mentioned how pirates \nenjoyed a tacit, quasi-religious legitimacy. This is not to suggest that the \nResident saw the connection of piracy with the temple at Dwarka as central; \nprobably, all that he intended to communicate was that raids and coastal \npolitics were implicated in a complex local economy of religion, markets, and \npolitics. However, the description stuck and it subsequently became part of \nan orientalizing strategy that tended to tag religion onto local customary \npractice. For the moment, it invoked a particular context in which activities \nsuch as predation were anchored within a local economy of protection, \nconvention, and customary obligations. It is important not to exaggerate \nthe religious overtones of the discourse; European observers spoke of the \nDwarka temple and its trustees as silent endorsers of piratical campaigns \nwhereas, in fact, what they were alluding to was the complicated caste and \npollution issues that marked off the Okha chieftains from the rest of their \nRajput brethren. In any case, Walker's nuanced ethnography did little to \nconvince his superiors about the Northern pirates, who were dismissed as \nsavage, pathologically prone to predation and criminal activity.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
          "source_file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 370869,
          "end_char": 372292,
          "start_line": 6989,
          "end_line": 7007,
          "printed_page": null,
