      {
        "finding_id": "section-6ff11501c137470529ca",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Many ofthose who were captured or accused of simple piracy had excuses \nat the ready as well. For instance, the janissary Mustafa Bese bin Abdullah \naccused the Armenian Yorgi veled Anton of the island of Kos of having \npartaken in a piratical attack on his ship four years earlier when he sued him \nin the court of Galata in April 1616. Returning from a trading expedition to \nEgypt, Mustafa Bese’s ship had dropped anchor at a spot along the coast near \nKos and the crew had tucked in for the night when Yorgi and his compatriots \nclimbed over the gunwales, seized Mustafa and his crew, robbed them, \nand plundered the ship. They did this, Mustafa explained, “because the \naforementioned Yorgi is a frigateer ( firkateci).\" But Yorgi defended himself \nby claiming that he himself had been the prisoner of a pirate, a notorious \n\"frigateer\" known as Ak Mehmed, and that it was Ak Mehmed who had \ndirected the assault on Mustafa Bese’s ship. Yorgi claimed that he had not \neven participated in the raid and that he had been chained hand and foot in \nAk Mehmed's frigate at the time of the attack.*° Yorgi's denial echoed that \nof countless pirates, who claimed that they were simple sailors who had no \nknowledge of what the captain had planned, or that they were prisoners \nforced to participate under duress.*7",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1616
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
