        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Islands were particularly troublesome as there was a constant give and \ntake between the state and pirates. Pirate islands once subdued were incor- \nporated into the legal realm ofthe inner ocean only to be later reoccupied by \nnew gangs of pirates, thereby relegating them once again to the ambiguous \nrealm of the outer ocean. Between Zhejiang and Guangdong there were \nseveral thousands of offshore islands, most of which remained uncharted \nand unnamed. Outside the gaze ofthe state, for centuries pirates established",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
