      {
        "finding_id": "section-61b9e44daadca8bf0982",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "autonomous communities on remote islands, where they erected cottages, \nsettled their families, and conducted business. The waters around the black \nmarket of Jiangping (Map 2), situated on the ill-defined Sino-Vietnamese \nborder, had served for centuries as an important rendezvous for pirates, \nsmugglers, and traders from China, Southeast Asia, and Europe. Jiangping \nwas on the major trading route between northern Vietnam and southern \nChina. The area's many craggy islands, sandy shoals, and hidden bays offered \nperfect hideaways for pirates and smugglers, yet were in easy reach of the \nblack market in Jiangping. In the Ming dynasty, at the entrance to the \nharbour a large Vietnamese squatter population of fisherfolk had settled on \nthe sandy shoals, and on the many islands dotting the outer ocean pirates \nestablished strongholds. Many of Jiangping's residents and fisherfolks actu- \nally specialized in handling stolen goods and provisioning pirates. Mindful \nof the issue of territorial sovereignty with its tributary neighbour, seldom \ndid China's naval forces venture into these waters; as late as the 1820s, the \nnearest government fortification was several hundred kilometres to the \neast. This was a troublesome area that the Qing government preferred \nto leave alone.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
          "source_file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 462671,
          "end_char": 463959,
          "start_line": 8659,
          "end_line": 8676,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
