        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "12 Guangdong haifang huilan [A conspectus of Guangdong’s coastal defense] (Canton, \nnineteenth century ed.), vol. 26, 1b-2a; and Robert Antony, “Giang Binh: Pirate Haven and \nBlack Market on the Sino-Vietnamese Frontier, 1780-1802,” in Pirates, Ports, and Coasts in Asia: \nHistorical and Contemporary Perspectives, ed. by John Kleinen and Manon Osseweijer (Leiden: \nInternational Institute for Asian Studies, 2010), 31-50. Based on the author's fieldwork in Jiangping \nin January 2010 and August 201, the area is still a major smuggling zone and Jiangping remains \nan important black market.",
