        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "not its concern. The defensive land-centred strategy precluded building a \nblue-water navy capable of operating effectively on the high seas or outer \nocean.’ This, of course, was very different from European states, which at \nroughly the same time were earnestly building blue-water navies to protect \ntheir merchant fleets from pirates and rival countries in waters far away \nfrom home.'^ Thus from imperial China's perspective, oceans - especially \nthe outer ocean - were a lawless, dangerous, and uncivilized space, a “dark \nrealm\" of pirates, rebels, and other lawbreakers.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
