        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "rather they were penned by a nineteenth-century Spanish historian of \nmilitary background, Pio de Pazos y Vela Hidalgo (1841-1913), who personally \nparticipated in an expedition against Mindanao rebels in 1866. They were \npart ofa chronological account of what he called a Military History of Jolo. \nIt is an apt introductory quote reflecting both the key topoi and muddled \nchronologies of the history of piracy in the Spanish Philippines.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
