      {
        "finding_id": "section-0849524fe4549f10feb0",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "in the Great Northern War (1700-1721). King Karl XIT's (r. 1697—1718) attempt at \nBaltic mastery had only recently ended in catastrophe at Poltava in 1709. Over \nthe following years, he lived as a monarch in exile in the distant Ottoman \nEmpire. Sweden's once mighty army meanwhile had been dispersed and all \nbut destroyed, state finances were in ruin, and the navy decayed. Swedish \nmerchant shipping, so desperately important to restore national finances, \nlay exposed to piratical threats and to rivalry with other European pow- \ners. In this context, Thelaus's choice of dissertation reflects a concern not \njust for scholarly rhetoric but contemporary national and world events. So \ndesperate had Sweden's plight become that state officials were considering \ncollaborating with the pirates of Madagascar to secure ships and to protect \nforeign trade, even perhaps gaining a pirate colony in the bargain. Hence, \nThelaus's argument in De piratica that attitudes to piracy should be shaped \nby both moral stipulations and expedient calculations of advantage is of \nsignificant interest.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1697,
          1700
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
          "source_file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 582617,
          "end_char": 583707,
