        "evidence_excerpt": "force, rising up against the established authority?? - also implied a person \nwho was beyond the borders of law and civilization. The term, however, \ndid not necessarily imply an activity at sea or close to the sea, and, as with \nthe word Aài [sea] in Mandarin, it was added as an affix to gidc in order to \nmark that such a person or activities occurred at sea. According to a late \nnineteenth-century Annamite-French dictionary, the term hai giác was \nthus translated to French as “maritime war, pirates, corsairs.””*",
