        "evidence_excerpt": "continued to be problematic on land for another ten years, although the \nsea pirates in the Gulf of Tonkin — who, a couple of decades earlier, had \nflourished on the trafficking of Vietnamese to China and European ports \nin East Asia — by the early 1890s were described as consisting of very small \nand poor groups and lacking in maritime capacity.4?",
