        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The Vietnamese word that most closely resembled the French pirate was, \nas discussed above, gidc, and by associating all those who resisted French \ncolonisation — including both the Black Flags and other bandits and the \nCan Vuong movement - the French could tap into a long-standing tradition \namong Vietnamese mandarins of defaming any rebellion or challenge to \nthe established order and authority. By framing the military operations \nagainst all who resisted French colonisation as anti-piracy or anti-gidc \noperations, the French thus aimed to legitimise their repression in Vietnam \nwith reference to the Confucian order.^?",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
          "source_file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
