        "evidence_excerpt": "Overly literal readings of the rhetoric of pirates as the enemies of all \nmankind would matter less if they did not obstruct our view ofthe tensions \npervading European imperial policies. Consider the multiplicity of views \namong Europeans in discussing piracy and anti-piracy measures in early \nnineteenth century Southeast Asia. An uptick in sea raiding and slaving \nprompted British and Dutch officials to voice concerns about the effects",
