        "evidence_excerpt": "Asian waters, Subramanian describes raiding as endemic on the Western \nIndian littoral, and the editors remark on the ubiquity of raiding in Europe.” \n\"Slaving piracy” was a particular and widespread kind of raiding.5? Broadly, \nraiding was associated with coastal militarization and the construction \nof forts — both trends that predated European maritime violence and also \nintensified as a result of European incursions.5*",
