      {
        "finding_id": "section-21eae9142badb767811d",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Once  the  \"  Grand  Period \"  was  passed,  that \nperiod  in  which  such  men  as  the  Barbarossas, \nDragut,  and  Ali  flourished,  the  chronicle  of  the \nMoslem  States  founded  by  them  sinks  to  the  de- \ngraded level  of  sheer  'robbery  and  murder ;  of  a \nhistory  of  a  tyranny  established  within  one  hundred \nmiles  of  the  shores  of  Europe,  and  of  great  kings \nand  princes  bargaining  with  piratical  ruffians  who \nheld  in  thrall  thousands  upon  thousands  of  their \nsubjects.  How  it  came  about  that  the  Christian \nStates  tolerated  such  an  abuse  is  one  of  those  mys- \nteries which  can  never  be  explained ;  and  if  sub- \nsequent centuries  displayed  a  greater  refinement  of \nmanners,  a  more  apt  appreciation  of  all  that  is \nsofter  and  kindlier  in  the  human  relationships  of \nnation  towards  nation  and  of  people  towards  people, \nthey  have  not  perhaps  so  much  to  plume  themselves \nupon  as  had  their  rude  forefathers  of  the  sixteenth \ncentury,  who,  seeing  the  evil  and  feeling  the  effects \nthereof,  did  their  best  to  extirpate  those  by  whom \nthis  evil  was  caused.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
