      {
        "finding_id": "section-5daceb4538aaadeb87ad",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "their  Christian  contemporaries  ;  that  they  had  been \ndriven  with  fire  and  sword  from  the  land  in  which \nthey  and  their  forefathers  had  dwelt  for  over  seven \ncenturies,  and  that  they  now  had  been  cast  out  liter- \nally to  starve  on  the  inhospitable  shores  of  North- \nern Africa.  So  it  came  about  that  the  common \npeople  exchanged  the  life  of  the  peaceful  and  pros- \nperous artisan  or  husbandman  for  that  of  the  hand- \nto-mouth  pirate,  and  the  case  of  knight  and  noble \namong  them  was  no  better — perhaps  rather  worse \n— than  the  meanest  among  those  who  had  been \nexpropriated.",
