      {
        "finding_id": "section-c9b17b43c8adbf04091e",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "It  was  shortly  after  the  death  of  his  brother \nUruj  that  the  storm  arose  which  bade  fair  to  sweep, \nnot  only  Kheyr-ed-Din  but  all  the  corsairs  of  the \nNorth  African  coast,  clean  out  of  their  strong- \nholds, for  the  Emperor  Charles  V.,  at  this  time \nyoung,  eager,  and  enthusiastic,  gave  orders  for  their \ndestruction.  These  robbers  troubled  the  peace  of \nEurope  ;  they  did  more  than  this,  they  insulted \nthe  Majesty  of  the  Emperor,  and  Charles  regarded \ntheir  perpetual  incursions  in  the  light  of  an  affront \nto  his  personal  dignity.  The  divinity  which  hedged \nsuch  a  monarch  as  the  grandson  of  \"  Los  Reyes \nCatolicos,\"  Ferdinand  and  Isabella,  was  a  very  real \nthing,  and,  if  offended,  was  likely  to  find  concrete \nexpression  in  the  most  vigorous  form.  Charles, \nmuch  annoyed  at  the  necessity  for  chastising  a  band \nof  robbers,  determined  that  he  would  make  an  end  of \nthem  once  and  for  all.  To  Don  Hugo  de  Moncada, \nthe  Viceroy  of  Sicily,  to  Don  Perisan  de  Ribera  at \nBougie,  to  the  Marquis  de  Comares  at  Oran,  orders \nwere  sent  to  prepare  their  forces  for  an  attack  on \nAlgiers.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
