      {
        "finding_id": "section-dc206d42574c45fc9c9c",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Forty  sail  in  strength,  they  set  out  to  avenge  the \nwrongs  of  the  gentle  and  long-suffering  Kheyr-ed- \nDin,  that  master  of  craft  in  every  sense  of  the \nword.  Reaching  Algiers,  they  disembarked  artil- \nlery and  stores  and  began  an  attack  in  form  ;  but \nVenalcadi,  whose  forces  were  equal,  in  fact  slightly \nsuperior,  to  those  of  his  antagonists,  made  a  sally, \nand  battle  was  joined  in  the  open.  A  most  san- \nguinary combat  ensued,  in  which  the  forces  of \nKheyr-ed-Din  were  decidedly  worsted.  For  a \nconsiderable  period  his  fate  hung  in  the  balance. \nThen  occurred  one  of  those  singular  and  remark- \nable things  only  possible  in  such  an  age  of  anarchy \nand  bloodshed.  Barbarossa  had  in  his  train  sixty \nSpanish  soldiers  captured  by  him  from  the  force \nof  Don  Hugo  de  Moncada.  Well  did  the  corsair \nknow  their  value :  there  were  no  finer  fighting \nmen  in  all  the  Christian  armies.  Hastily  sum- \nmoning them,  he  promised  them  their  freedom  if \nthey  would  now  throw  in  their  lot  with  him  and \nassist  in  the  downfall  of  Venalcadi.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
          "source_file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
