        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "hampered  by  his  sense  of  responsibility  as  Admiral- \nissimo  to  the  Grand  Turk.  What  happened  on \nthe  distant  shores  of  Africa  mattered  but  little  to \nthat  monarch,  and  he  had  been  content  to  allow  his \nadmiral  an  entirely  free  hand ;  here  in  Europe, \non  the  shores  of  Greece,  so  close  relatively  to  his \nown  capital  city,  it  was  a  very  different  matter, \nand  Soliman  was  kept  in  touch  with  the  happenings \nof  his  fleet  as  far  as  was  possible  in  those  days. \nBut  if  the  great  corsair  did  not  add  to  his  reputation \nin  this  eventful  campaign  he  still  displayed  an \naptitude  in  realising  the  situation  which,  it  is \nsafe  to  say,  was  shown  by  none  of  those  under  his \ncommand.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
