      {
        "finding_id": "section-be4936b00422dfc3b723",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "With  such  skill  and  address  did  the  corsair \nmanage  his  suit  that  he  prevailed  upon  the  Sul- \ntan to  address  a  letter  to  Charles  demanding  the \nimmediate  return  of  the  towns  of  Susa,  Sfax,  Mon- \nastir,  and  \"  Africa.\"  This,  of  course,  meant  war ; \nas  Charles  immediately  replied  that  these  places \nwere  dependencies  of  the  King  of  Tunis,  and  that \nthat  ruler  was  under  his  special  protection  ;  further \nthat  they  were  his  by  right  of  conquest ;  finally \nthat  the  matter  was  no  concern  whatever  of  the \nSultan  of  Constantinople.  The  stern  and  imperi- \nous Christian  Emperor  was  in  no  mood  to  brook \ninterference,  the  more  so  that  he  discerned  plainly \nthat  though  the  demand  was  that  of  Soliman,  the \nmover  in  the  affair  was  none  other  than  Dragut. \nHe  therefore  by  way  of  a  rider  to  his  answer  to \nthe  Sultan  informed  that  monarch  that  these  places \nwhich  he  had  taken  on  the  coast  of  Africa  had \nbeen  reft  by  him  \"  from  one  Dragut,  a  corsair \nodious  to  both  God  and  man  \" ;  that  without  in \nany  way  departing  from  the  treaty  which  he  had \nmade  with  Soliman  \"  he  intended  to  pursue  this \npirate  whithersoever  he  might  go.\"",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
