        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Having  thus  restored  order  to  the  finances,  the \nGrand  Master  turned  his  attention  to  the  state \nof  affairs  (as  he  had  received  them  from  his  pre- \ndecessor) connected  with  the  territorial  possessions \nof  the  Knights.  For  long  years  now  the  fortress \nof  Tripoli  had  been  in  the  hands  of  the  renowned \nDragut,  who  was  the  scourge  and  the  terror  of  the \nChristians.  The  corsair  dwelt  in  his  stronghold  in \ninsolent  defiance  of  the  Knights,  whose  property \nit  once  had  been.  Years  before  he  had  wrested  it \nfrom  them  by  the  strong  hand :  what,  then,  more \nnecessary  in  the  eyes  of  such  an  one  as  La  Valette \nthan  to  expel  this  audacious  pirate  ?  The  Grand",
