          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Point  of  the  Gallows,  because  it  was  here  that  all \npirates  were  executed ;  and  their  bodies,  swinging  in \nchains,  were  the  first  objects  that  met  the  eye  on \nentering  the  Great  Port).  In  this  he  was  over- \nruled by  Piali,  who  declared  that  he  had  not  sufficient \nmen  to  spare,  and  the  Knights  of  II  Borgo  would \nsoon  render  the  battery  untenable  even  if  they \nshould  succeed  in  erecting  it,  which  the  Turkish \nadmiral  now  considered  extremely  doubtful.  The \nsiege  of  St.  Elmo,  which  Mustafa  had  said  would \nlast  at  the  outside  for  five  or  six  days,  had  now  been \nin  progress  for  four  weeks ;  and,  although  the  fort \nwas  in  a  ruinous  condition,  nothing  seemed  capable \nof  daunting  those  invincible  warriors  by  which  it \nwas  held.",
