      {
        "finding_id": "section-1521086aee40f8f0f228",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "I  have  heard  several  mariners  and  cap- \ntains  of  the  sea,  nay,  even  Knights  of \nMalta,  debate  among  themselves  this  question,  as \nto  which  was  the  greater  and  better  seaman,  Dragut \nor  Occhiali  ?  And  some  held  for  one  and  some  for \nthe  other  ;  those  who  held  for  Occhiali  declaring \nthat  he  had  held  greater  and  more  honourable \ncharges  than  Dragut,  because  he  commanded  as \nGeneral  and  Admiral  for  the  Grand  Turk  and  that \nil  fit  belle  action  at  the  battle  of  Lepanto.\"  Pierre \nde  Bourdeille,  the  Seigneur  de  Brant  ome,  from \nwhom  we  make  the  above  quotation,  was  himself \npresent  at  the  siege  of  Malta  and,  besides  this,  as  is \nwell  known,  gossiped  in  his  own  inimitable  way  con- \ncerning men  and  women  of  his  time,  from  corsairs \nto  courtesans.  When  such  contemporary  authori- \nties as  those  mentioned  could  not  agree  it  is  quite \ncertain  that  we  of  the  twentieth  century  cannot \ndecide  on  the  rival  claims  to  distinction  between \nthe  Bashaw  of  Tripoli  and  his  follower  Occhiali, \nas  he  was  known  to  the  Christians,  or  Ali  Basha,",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
